This is extra information for ScriptBasic when building and running on
Apple macOS (Darwin).

macOS is treated as a flavour of UNIX and ScriptBasic builds as a
command-line tool just like on Linux or FreeBSD. The setup script detects
macOS automatically; you can also specify it with the option --darwin of
setup.pl.

The build creates the interpreter scriba, the web server sbhttpd and the
library libscriba.a, as well as the extension modules as .dylib files in
the directory bin/mod/dll.

Note that the third party libraries needed by some extension modules
(MySQL, PostgreSQL, curl, libxml2, zlib, ...) have to be installed
separately, for example using Homebrew or MacPorts. Only the extension
modules whose libraries are present will be built.

The ScriptBasic interpreter is licenced LGPL. The text of the licence can be found
in the file License.txt

Some of the modules use code from different projects thus they may be licensed different.
